# Rust
/target/
/target_host/
# Fuzzing: targets and seeds are source and belong in review. Keeping the whole
# directory out is why `pack()` could grow two parameters and leave
# fuzz_wire_payload_roundtrip uncompilable without anyone noticing.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/Cargo.lock
/benches
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS tracked: construct-core ships inside a signed binary, so the
# dependency set must be reproducible and auditable (cargo-audit reads this file).
# construct-veil / -transport / -server all track theirs; this one was an oversight.

# A machine's Android NDK pin. It was tracked, with one developer's absolute
# NDK path, and went stale on every NDK update: SDK Manager replaces the
# side-by-side NDK, and the path then pointed at nothing. Nothing needs it —
# construct-android's build_crypto_lib.sh finds the NDK itself and passes the
# linker and ar through CARGO_TARGET_<TRIPLE>_LINKER/_AR (env beats this
# file), and CI builds through cargo-ndk. A local copy may stay; it is yours.
/.cargo/config.toml

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# macOS
.DS_Store

